Z||000000||Monkeyman||11-18-2001||12:21 PM||||I'm interested in the Mk III ('86-'9?) Supras.  They were my 2<sup>nd</sup> choice after the Fiero.  I don't necessarily want to get rid of the Fiero (it will always be my #1, most favoritestest car in the entire world), but the Supra still interestes me.  <P>Info?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/patriot.gif">    <BR><B><FONT COLOR="red">Proud</FONT> <FONT COLOR="white">to be an</FONT> <FONT COLOR="blue">American</FONT>!!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Spektrum-87GT||11-18-2001||01:01 PM||||nice looking, dependable, cool interior, awesome targa top, VERY fast, only drawback... EXPENSIVE!!!<P>i've yet to see a 91 turbo go for less than 5k(in decent shape). I was considering getting one for a while also, they're really sweet cars, i prefer the 4th gen but i dont prefer the price on them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>the one thing i've noticed about the 3rd gen supras is that they last forever!!! must be that toyota inline 6.||||reg||1
