Z||000012||Monkeyman||11-19-2001||04:21 PM||||From what I've read, 170k miles on a Supra is like 60k on a Fiero.  Makes you wonder what Toyota does that GM can't copy.  The few Supra owners I know have lots and lots of miles on their cars and have never really had any major problems.  Like I posted earlier, I'd be looking for a loaded, non-turbo car (unless a nice turbo came up cheap).  I could always upgrade motors in the future if I felt the need.  I can vaguely remember test driving a brand new '87 or '88 non turbo.  Seemed like it had decent power.  About the same as a stock 2.8 Fiero (although they say the memory is the 1<sup>st</sup> to go).||||reg||1
Z||000013||SwissFormula||11-19-2001||05:51 PM||||Cool cars, i like them too. Try to find a '90 or newer supra, they have better brakes (less fading) and some other mods i can't remember right now.<P>------------------<BR>Roy<P>88 Formula, T-Top<BR>1 of 20 Fieros in Switzerland||||reg||14
Z||000014||Master_Sushi||11-19-2001||08:32 PM||||I love MK3 supras!!! I have been trying to decide what care im going to get next, mk3 supra or a mint Fiero gt. I'm starting to lean towards the supra. Here what I like about them. A quality jap engine that puts out over 230 turbocharged hp. I love the way they look, targa tops are great. They have a big aftermarket background so its easy to mod them up to insane street machines. They are very high quality cars. I've heard they are built like tanks. They are VERY luxurious and are loaded with options. Even the base models had everything a loaded Fiero comes with.<BR>Only things to look out for are bad head gaskets, this was the only big problem with the car. Oh, and I've read monkeyman that the engines on the turbo models are built better on the turbo versions. So if you ever want a turbo its best to get one from the factory, or plan on a whole engine swap. Try <A HREF="http://www.supraforums.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.supraforums.com</A>  , its just like this forum. Make sure you in the MK3 area though.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000015||Master_Sushi||11-20-2001||11:38 AM||||Anyone in this forum ever own a mk3 supra?? If so I want to know what you thought of it?! I've been reading about supras for years now, but would like to know what a forum member thinkgs of them. Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
